 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd and ironic. No animal is shown hurt or handled roughly: the pigeon lands on a barrier arm and rests in a ventilated carrier; the Colombian pigeon flutters down to the pavement; the cat sits in a torch beam. No weapon, no violence. The customs officer, the police officer, the prison guard and the young man in the lesson are generic figures, never named; no badge, flag, patch, crest or insignia of any real force; no agency logo. Prison and agency names are plain text only. Drugs are shown only as plain pills, a taped bundle and a small packet. The drug in the Kuwaiti backpack is disputed (ketamine per al-Rai via the BBC; ecstasy per other outlets): narration says 'pills', the screen says 'reportedly a form of ketamine'. 'It did not ask for a lawyer' is a deadpan joke, not a claim. Every card is our own typed graphic. No dialogue is invented. Status verified 2026-10-17.",
