 "claims": [
  {
   "id": "K_hook",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "In May 2017 customs officers in Kuwait caught a pigeon carrying drugs (pills) in a small fabric pouch / 'miniature backpack' strapped to its back. Narration: 'This pigeon wore a backpack full of drugs.' Headline 'A PIGEON WITH A BACKPACK / FULL OF DRUGS'.",
   "sources": [
    "citi",
    "fox",
    "ifls",
    "vice",
    "fox13",
    "newarab"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_year",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The pigeon was caught in 2017 (reported 24-26 May 2017). Narration: 'In 2017. It did not ask for a lawyer.' (the second sentence is a deadpan joke, not a factual claim; no lawyer or charge is reported).",
   "sources": [
    "citi",
    "fox13",
    "fox",
    "newarab"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_catch",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The pigeon was caught by customs officers near the customs building in Abdali, close to the border with Iraq. Narration: 'Kuwaiti customs caught it near the Iraqi border.' Label 'ABDALI, KUWAIT · MAY 2017'.",
   "sources": [
    "citi",
    "fox",
    "ifls",
    "fox13"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_pills",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "STATISTIC (counter): the backpack held 178 pills (al-Rai, relayed by the BBC); an al-Rai journalist said they were a form of ketamine (some outlets reported ecstasy). Narration: 'What was in the backpack? 178 pills.' Label 'AL-RAI VIA BBC / Reportedly a form of ketamine'.",
   "sources": [
    "citi",
    "fox",
    "ifls",
    "vice"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_clumsy",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Editorial bridge to item 2 (another pigeon whose drug run failed because of its load). Narration: 'But that was not the clumsiest one.'",
   "sources": [
    "colrep",
    "time",
    "register",
    "wildcat"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_colombia",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "In January 2011 police in Bucaramanga, Colombia, found a pigeon carrying drugs (about 45 g: 40 g of marijuana and 5 g of cocaine paste, 'bazuco') about a block from a prison it was trying to reach. Narration: 'In Colombia, one tried flying drugs into a prison.'",
   "sources": [
    "colrep",
    "time",
    "register",
    "wildcat",
    "insight"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_sim",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "FUN FACT CARD: police said pigeons had previously been used to smuggle SIM cards into the same jail. Card 'PIGEONS HAD ALREADY FLOWN SIM CARDS INTO THAT JAIL'.",
   "sources": [
    "time",
    "colrep",
    "register"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_heavy",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Police said the package was too heavy for the bird to clear the prison walls (the local commander attributed the failure to the excess weight). Narration: 'Police said it was too heavy to clear the wall.' Label 'BUCARAMANGA, COLOMBIA · JAN 2011 / About 45 g of marijuana and cocaine paste'.",
   "sources": [
    "colrep",
    "time",
    "register",
    "wildcat"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_lesson",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "LESSON CARD (practical, for the viewer): criminal groups recruit people to carry drugs, sometimes offering money or a free trip to carry luggage or a parcel (UK Travel Aware, FCDO); do not carry items for someone else and be aware of the contents of your bags (Smartraveller). Rows: 'CARRY ONLY YOUR OWN BAGS', 'KNOW WHAT IS INSIDE THEM', 'PAID TO CARRY? RED FLAG'.",
   "sources": [
    "aware",
    "smart",
    "smart_d"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_cat",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "On 1 August 2020 jail intelligence officers at Welikada Prison, Sri Lanka, caught a cat with a small plastic bag tied around its neck holding nearly two grams of heroin, two SIM cards and a memory chip. Narration: 'Sri Lanka caught a cat smuggling heroin into prison.' Label 'WELIKADA PRISON, SRI LANKA · AUG 2020'.",
   "sources": [
    "inquirer",
    "gulf",
    "newdaily",
    "ftlk",
    "observer",
    "vice_cat"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_share",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Share prompt (no factual claim). Narration: 'Send this to the mate who feeds pigeons.'",
   "sources": [
    "citi",
    "colrep"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_caught",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "All three animals were caught: the Kuwaiti pigeon by customs, the Colombian pigeon by police, the Sri Lankan cat by jail officials. Narration: 'All three got caught.'",
   "sources": [
    "citi",
    "fox",
    "colrep",
    "time",
    "inquirer",
    "observer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_escape",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The cat escaped the next day (2 August 2020) from the room in the prison where it was held. Narration (LAST line): 'Only the cat broke out of jail.' Label 'THE CAT ESCAPED THE NEXT DAY / Sri Lanka, Aug 2020 · via AFP'.",
   "sources": [
    "inquirer",
    "gulf",
    "newdaily",
    "ftlk",
    "observer",
    "vice_cat"
   ]
  }
 ],
